feat(ui): iOS-style push/pop slide and 17sp navigation titles

DESIGN_SPEC sections 6 and 11.

- CubicBezierInterpolator: new IOS_SLIDE curve (0.33, 0.52, 0.25, 0.99),
  the iOS slide curve from ContainedViewLayoutTransition.swift.
- ActionBarLayout: the standard (non-preview) push now slides the new
  screen in over the full width, and pop slides it out over the full
  width, with no fade. It uses IOS_SLIDE and 350 ms instead of a 48dp
  fade with DecelerateInterpolator over 150 ms. Preview (long-press)
  animations are unchanged. The iOS parallax shift and dimming of the
  screen below are not added.
- ActionBar: title text is 17sp in all modes (iOS nav title 17pt). The
  glass mode already used 17.

The 350 ms duration is a gap in DESIGN_SPEC (not found in the iOS code);
it is the UIKit default and is listed in PROGRESS.md.
